## Context
The author, 2026-11-12, verbatim: *"retire this repository's `.claude/rules/`
directory. Every runtime we use (Claude Code, Codex, Pi) now reads AGENTS.md
natively, but only Claude Code reads `.claude/rules/`, so those rules are
invisible to the others. Merge their content into AGENTS.md and delete the
directory."*

The three rule files (`bench.md`, `documents.md`, `tickets.md`) were each
path-scoped by `paths:` frontmatter. Their content moves into `AGENTS.md` as
sections headed by the paths they govern, merged rather than pasted: what
`AGENTS.md` already says is not repeated, dated incident narratives shrink to
the mechanism they taught.

## Exit criteria
- [ ] `.claude/rules/` deleted; `.gitignore` no longer excepts it
- [ ] Every project-specific requirement of the three files appears in an
      `AGENTS.md` section headed by its original `paths:`
- [ ] `git grep -n '.claude/rules'` returns only history records
      (`DECISIONS.md`, `tickets/closed/`, this ticket)
- [ ] The retirement is recorded in `DECISIONS.md` in the author's words
- [ ] `make check-diff` green, `selected:`/`skipped:` quoted on the PR
